1
00:00:14,830 --> 00:00:17,960
Rikukaikuu doko ni ikou

2
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:20,420
Ahiru no Sora

3
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:21,040
Kimi o sasoitai na

4
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:25,880
Monogatari wa hajima tterunda

5
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:31,580
Okubyou kaze mo recycle

6
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:34,630
Mayotteru senaka oshite

7
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:39,790
Give and go! Isogou

8
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:47,920
Mogutteita honou ga kaodashite

9
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:55,130
Kakusenai no sa yume ni mita yume

10
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:58,540
Tobenai tsubasa demo

11
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:05,420
Bokura wa habataite sora o kanjitai

12
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,750
Naritai jibun ni naritai

13
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:15,420
Ima dekinai koto mo ashita wa wakannai ze

14
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:18,880
Waru agaki shiyou

15
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:21,920
Happy go ducky!

16
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:34,330
The 2-3 zone.

17
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:37,610
It's the most commonly used formation
when playing zone defense.

18
00:01:41,210 --> 00:01:42,500
My dear Nao...

19
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:47,040
I know that zone defense is full of your love,
so I'll fill our offense with my own.

20
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:49,710
Quit wasting time! Just get on with it!

21
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,380
Get your guard up, girls!

22
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:53,750
Here they come!

23
00:01:58,210 --> 00:01:58,920
Sweet.

24
00:01:59,210 --> 00:01:59,960
Got it?

25
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:03,540
Whenever you receive a pass,
you have to take stock of the situation around you.

26
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,810
Look for anybody who is open.
And check for empty space in front of you.

27
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,940
Okay! I'll handle this!

28
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,630
Hey, Yasu! Over here!

29
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,440
Nice, Chucky!

30
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:17,400
I've got him!

31
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,130
Sayuri!

32
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:23,740
Shit... I still can't dribble 
the ball properly...

33
00:02:27,330 --> 00:02:28,420
A screen!

34
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:29,790
Yoko, in the middle!

35
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,000
Over here!

36
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,790
Oh, Nabe is free!

37
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:41,210
Time is up! 24-second violation!

38
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:42,680
I totally forgot.

39
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:47,170
We only have 24 seconds to take a shot
when we're on offense, right?

40
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:50,130
Sorry, it's all because I was lagging behind.

41
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:51,920
Nah, you're doing fine as-is.

42
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:55,670
Don't try and rush it, just stay aware
of your surroundings.

43
00:02:55,960 --> 00:03:00,330
The role of each player in a zone defense
is much more ambiguous than in man-to-man.

44
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:04,620
So sometimes it's possible for them
to end up overlapping like you just saw.

45
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:08,170
And if two defenders end up
covering the same player, then what happens?

46
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:11,500
I get it, that means 
somebody else is left open.

47
00:03:11,670 --> 00:03:14,460
Their current zone defense
was hastily prepared to counter us.

48
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,710
Holes are bound to open up in it eventually.

49
00:03:18,170 --> 00:03:20,420
Momoharu and I will focus 
on making those holes.

50
00:03:20,830 --> 00:03:22,380
Make sure you watch closely.

51
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:31,290
Boys

52
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:31,290
Girls

53
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:31,000
Nice three-pointer, Yoko!

54
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,670
I just remembered something Kite said to us.

55
00:03:37,130 --> 00:03:39,150
Whenever we get the ball, 
we should always look at...

56
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:41,540
...the basket!

57
00:03:42,130 --> 00:03:44,110
What the hell is she doing?

58
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:46,830
H-he isn't going to take a shot...?

59
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:50,790
And now I blow past her. 
Is that how this works?

60
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,750
That was smooth! When did 
Yasu actually get that good?

61
00:03:55,830 --> 00:03:57,170
Gah! Oh shi-!

62
00:03:57,670 --> 00:03:59,130
Whoa there!

63
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,830
Nice one, Nabe!

64
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:05,210
What the hell are you passing
to the other team for, dumbass?!

65
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:08,170
Like you're one to talk, what 
kind of dribbling was that?!

66
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:08,180
Kurumatani: 3-Pointers, speed
Chucky: Calm and can analyze...
Nabe: Awarenes is...
Yasuhara: Ball handling needs...

67
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:12,790
When Yasu went for that drive just now,
it opened another hole in the defense.

68
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:13,830
Did you see it?

69
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,380
Yeah. I saw it.

70
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:18,830
Dummy! What were you thinking?!

71
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:20,480
The defender that was in front of me
took off to try and block Yasu.

72
00:04:20,710 --> 00:04:23,130
It left me totally free on the opposite side.

73
00:04:23,670 --> 00:04:27,880
The zone defense makes it relatively easy
for members of the offense to get open.

74
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:31,950
By repeating a cycle of passes and drives,
it will eventually fall apart.

75
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:45,430
Boys

76
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:45,430
Girls

77
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:50,380
It was a mistake to let him handle anything.
The other team is just widening the gap on us.

78
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:54,100
I'm starting to think that Bro had no idea
what he was doing this whole time.

79
00:04:54,710 --> 00:04:57,080
The only players without an idea
of what they're doing are you two.

80
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:04,000
The reason I said this team would never win,
is because you lack something very fundamental.

81
00:05:04,330 --> 00:05:05,710
"Something fundamental"?

82
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:06,460
Yep.

83
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:09,670
What every team needs
to deal with screens and zone defense,

84
00:05:10,170 --> 00:05:13,000
is absolute faith in each other's 
ability to provide cover.

85
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:18,960
Having players who think they can just use other skills
to cover their own weaknesses

86
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:21,630
prevents the team from 
functioning as a whole.

87
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:26,960
The one thing this team needs in order to win,

88
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,820
is for every player to embrace their own shortcomings.

89
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:33,390
Chiaki:
wide field of vision, passes 
 Everyone must embrace shortcomings
Must work on individual scoring
and making the best of situations
must learn how to coordinate
(screens and pass work)
(Overall) Lacking stamina
Refine fundamentals, especially footwork

90
00:05:30,170 --> 00:05:33,040
And then use teamwork to 
adequately make up for those.

91
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:36,710
You know what they say: 
There is no "I" in "TEAM."

92
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:38,850
That's a fundamental part of basketball.

93
00:05:45,690 --> 00:05:47,150
Okay! Do it now!

94
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:54,540
Somebody get on him!

95
00:05:58,670 --> 00:06:01,750
Incredible! He's totally free 
right in front of the basket!

96
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:04,210
A-amazing...

97
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:08,250
See that? Hope you're 
watching, little birdies!

98
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:10,710
I am a genius on the court!

99
00:06:16,350 --> 00:06:19,830
Boys

100
00:06:16,350 --> 00:06:19,830
Girls

101
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,000
Game over!

102
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,330
The girls' win with 18 points to 5!

103
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:22,290
All right!

104
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:25,420
Thank God! My body has been 
saved from ogling eyes!

105
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:30,920
Whoops! I totally spaced
that Momoharu can't shoot to save his life.

106
00:06:31,870 --> 00:06:37,710
Note: Lyrics from the 1974 enka 
song, "Showa Kare Susuki."

107
00:06:31,870 --> 00:06:37,710
We lost to poverty~!

108
00:06:37,710 --> 00:06:43,040
Hold up! We didn't lose to poverty or anything like that!
We lost to the girls' team!

109
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:46,670
Just forget about the inter-high or whatever.

110
00:06:46,670 --> 00:06:49,710
I don't think we could even
beat a team of kids from elementary school.

111
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,670
I've lost every last 
ounce of motivation, man.

112
00:06:52,670 --> 00:06:54,920
Uh, wait! Come on, you guys.

113
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:57,250
Yasuhara!

114
00:06:58,960 --> 00:06:59,880
Nabe?!

115
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,170
Chucky!

116
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:04,630
N-not good...

117
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:07,670
Momoharu, please say something 
to bring them around!

118
00:07:09,170 --> 00:07:13,420
Oh, jeez! All we have to do is get better
by practicing more!

119
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:14,830
Right, Nanao?

120
00:07:15,290 --> 00:07:16,130
Huh?

121
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,630
Wh-where did she go?

122
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,170
I screwed it up again.

123
00:07:23,670 --> 00:07:26,710
I really only meant for it to 
be a little test of their skill.

124
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:31,180
Making them lose motivation is the exact opposite
of what a manager is supposed to do, ugh...

125
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:34,330
I can't figure it out. 
Why am I so bad at this?

126
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,500
It's like I have no ability to learn fro-

127
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:40,850
How lame!

128
00:07:40,850 --> 00:07:44,540
She's like a manga character!
I've never seen anybody fall in the gutter for real!

129
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:45,250
Same!

130
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:46,290
Nanao!

131
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,500
Kurumatani...?

132
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:51,330
You left so fast, I thought 
something might be wrong.

133
00:07:52,130 --> 00:07:53,580
Here, you forgot this.

134
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:54,750
Thanks...

135
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:58,630
Wh-what happened to... your leg?

136
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:06,000
P-please accept my apologies.

137
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,250
It's no big deal.

138
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:10,550
My grandma makes me take care
of the cleaning all the time.

139
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:11,920
Not that.

140
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:13,790
That's not what I'm apologizing for.

141
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:19,210
In that match earlier, my strategy
totally singled you out on every play...

142
00:08:20,130 --> 00:08:23,190
Uh, that's okay, no need to apologize to me.

143
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:27,150
I know that's just what it 
takes to win the game, right?

144
00:08:27,630 --> 00:08:30,790
Well, I'm a bit on the obsessive side.

145
00:08:30,790 --> 00:08:34,030
I always throw everything I have into it,
without even thinking.

146
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:38,330
Back in middle school,
stuff like this happened to me so much.

147
00:08:39,130 --> 00:08:42,410
GIRLS'
BASKETBALL
DISTRICT TOURNAMENT

148
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:42,410
Like back before the semi-finals
of our district tournament...

149
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:46,130
Our frontcourt game is weak!
We need to shore ourselves up in the middle!

150
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:51,460
Kosugi

151
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:47,960
Should we leave the defense as-is?

152
00:08:48,170 --> 00:08:51,630
Yeah. We don't want to ruin our rhythm
by changing anything we don't have to.

153
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:54,800
U-um, I think that we should 
sub out numbers 4 and 5.

154
00:08:55,290 --> 00:08:56,330
Huh?

155
00:08:56,920 --> 00:09:00,710
There's not much time left,
so we should focus our defense in the paint.

156
00:09:01,170 --> 00:09:03,830
That's why we should put in taller players
like Matsuki and Taniguchi.

157
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:08,670
Don't be stupid! I'm the team captain
and Miyuki is the vice-captain!

158
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:10,920
Why should we ever sub out 
for two younger players?

159
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,780
B-but that's what we need to win...

160
00:09:13,130 --> 00:09:16,990
A manager like you has no right
to be making important calls like that!

161
00:09:17,630 --> 00:09:20,210
Just keep your nose out of 
this and your own business!

162
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:23,450
It should have been obvious to me...

163
00:09:23,630 --> 00:09:28,540
I was out of line telling the seniors to sub out
for freshmen at such a crucial moment.

164
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:33,210
There are a lot of other important things to consider
than just winning and losing.

165
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:34,710
For sure...

166
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:40,420
Honestly, I think I'm better off just as a spectator
than being a part of the team.

167
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:43,880
My motive for wanting to join
was kind of immodest, anyway.

168
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:44,580
Huh?

169
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:46,750
Keep doing your best out there.

170
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:49,880
I think your team... will be 
a force to be reckoned with.

171
00:09:50,290 --> 00:09:51,750
Nanao...

172
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:53,170
Ouch!

173
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,580
Is she really gonna be okay?

174
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:01,380
She forgot it again?!

175
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:17,540
I think... she meant that she 
was going to quit the team.

176
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:20,750
No... say it ain't so!

177
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:25,350
Tell me, how am I supposed 
to keep on living now?

178
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:26,830
Who cares?

179
00:10:27,170 --> 00:10:28,750
Let her quit if she wants.

180
00:10:29,130 --> 00:10:32,750
We don't need a manager who wastes time
pretending to be a coach.

181
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:34,830
You don't have to be so rude about it.

182
00:10:34,830 --> 00:10:37,170
Nanao was just trying 
her best to help us all!

183
00:10:37,170 --> 00:10:41,250
To make a good coach,
you pretty much have to be a former player.

184
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:44,670
It's years of experience
that give a coach sufficient insight.

185
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:49,540
I'm not going to let a brat with no first-hand
experience tell me how to play the game.

186
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:53,090
That's not fair, she told us she was
on a basketball team back in middle school!

187
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:57,040
Yeah, but she was still just a manager.

188
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:59,330
The only thing a manager should do is take care

189
00:10:59,330 --> 00:11:01,230
of the odd jobs that nobody else has time for.

190
00:11:02,330 --> 00:11:04,460
Why do you always have 
to be such an asshole?!

191
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:05,790
Have some decency!

192
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,710
What? You wanna take this outside, shrimp?

193
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:15,150
What's all this?

194
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:17,630
They're notes from our game...

195
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:21,750
Whoa, this is nuts! There's 
more than 20 pages of stuff!

196
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:27,000
"Yasuhara has a good sense for driving,
but must work on improving his handling of the ball."

197
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:30,000
Hey! Is there anything about me in there?

198
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,750
Dude, I'm looking at what she wrote about me.
Just wait a damn minute!

199
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:34,210
That takes me back. She was 
always doing stuff like that.

200
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:38,790
I can tell you about Nao.
There's one part of her story that you don't know yet.

201
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:43,290
The truth is, she's been playing basketball
ever since she was a kid.

202
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:44,670
Huh?

203
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:47,670
She switched to being a manager
in the summer of her 2nd year at middle school.

204
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:50,630
Up until then, she practiced with us
as a member of the team.

205
00:11:51,170 --> 00:11:54,290
She switched? Because of an injury or what?

206
00:11:54,290 --> 00:11:56,500
Nope. She was in perfect shape.

207
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:58,920
I don't recall her ever suffering an injury.

208
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,210
But then, why the change?

209
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:04,830
She just wasn't suited to... 
the game of basketball.

210
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,420
Just think about it.

211
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:11,210
Sora is a good example of someone
who doesn't have the stature necessary for basketball,

212
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:14,960
but his speedy footwork and great shooting sense
make up for that disadvantage.

213
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:19,830
Naturally, we know that's the result of him
going through a lot of blood, sweat, and tears.

214
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:25,580
But some people in the world can never make up
the difference, no matter how hard they try.

215
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:30,220
Nao was one of them and that's why
she desperately tried to find her own path,

216
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:32,830
and eventually armed herself
with the weapon we call "strategy."

217
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:36,000
She read a ton of basketball books,

218
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,500
watched an endless amount of games,

219
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:41,990
and constantly scouted out
our opponents from other schools.

220
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:45,460
Unfortunately, her suggestions did lead
to some fights among the team,

221
00:12:45,830 --> 00:12:48,500
but her analysis of the 
situation was never wrong.

222
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:53,130
She didn't become the manager of your team
just to do a bunch of odd jobs.

223
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:57,500
She wants to be involved in the sport she loves,
in any way that she can.

224
00:12:58,380 --> 00:12:59,960
Is that really such a terrible thing?

225
00:13:05,630 --> 00:13:09,040
Awesome! That means she 
has incredible talent!

226
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:13,040
Nanao accomplished exactly what Kite was talking about
by dedicating herself

227
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:18,420
to mastering all of the knowledge that
a top-notch coach would have after years of play!

228
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:22,130
You guys should hurry and chase after her.

229
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,130
She's going to be your manager, right?

230
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:25,290
R-right.

231
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,240
Senpai...

232
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:30,420
Please let me use the showers
in the girl's changing room!

233
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:32,210
What the heck happened to you?!

234
00:13:33,170 --> 00:13:37,250
I was catching crayfish with some kids
when I fell into the water...

235
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,880
Yo. Thanks for this.

236
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,750
Wait, how did you...?

237
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,790
You forgot it back at the park.

238
00:13:47,250 --> 00:13:49,720
Seriously, this is downright incredible.

239
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,840
You didn't just lay out all of our failings,

240
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,980
you also made detailed notes on how we can fix them.

241
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:59,330
If we practice all that stuff you wrote down,
will we get better?

242
00:13:59,330 --> 00:14:01,940
If there's anything else we 
can do, let us know, yeah?

243
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:06,250
My dear Nao, you don't 
have to do a thing for me.

244
00:14:06,250 --> 00:14:07,420
Just having you here is enough to-

245
00:14:07,420 --> 00:14:09,540
Why are you the only one going full creeper?!

246
00:14:12,250 --> 00:14:14,630
I hope you'll do more 
than just be our manager.

247
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:16,460
Let's play together sometime!

248
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:20,170
I know you can play basketball,
so it would be a waste not to!

249
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,130
Are you sure?

250
00:14:26,330 --> 00:14:28,080
Can I really be your manager?

251
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,170
Of course!

252
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,170
Real talk though, our 
advisor is a total noob.

253
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:40,230
You'd be saving our asses
if you could act as our coach, too.

254
00:14:40,830 --> 00:14:42,750
I'm a pretty strict coach, you know.

255
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,790
Great. That's exactly what we need.

256
00:14:45,330 --> 00:14:46,750
Hey, little lady.

257
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:52,000
Don't you dare think that you got the better of me
with that weakass zone defense of yours.

258
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:54,580
Just watch this.

259
00:14:57,290 --> 00:14:59,000
A 3-pointer...?

260
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,960
Seriously? He can shoot from long-range, too?

261
00:15:02,710 --> 00:15:05,540
I was subbed out before I had the chance
to bring my A-game.

262
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:08,670
I never lost to you or your strategy, got it?

263
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,230
In that case, I would have tweaked our zone

264
00:15:11,230 --> 00:15:13,510
and shut you down with the triangle and 2 defense!

265
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,460
This damn half-pint...!

266
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:21,920
This cocky pineapple head...!

267
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,500
Uh, let's get along please! No fighting!

268
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:31,860
Go!

269
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:36,670
Hey, Nabe! You need to react faster!

270
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:37,330
Okay!

271
00:15:37,330 --> 00:15:38,630
Round 12!

272
00:15:38,630 --> 00:15:41,330
You're not allowed to turn 
around until you hear me clap!

273
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:44,420
Keep your hands up in the air
until you hear me give the sign!

274
00:15:45,830 --> 00:15:48,130
No lying down during the intervals!

275
00:15:48,130 --> 00:15:50,880
Please keep your breathing 
steady with a light jog!

276
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:52,890
She's a demon...

277
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:53,830
A dictator...

278
00:15:53,830 --> 00:15:56,850
Since the volleyball team has the gym
today we had no other choice,

279
00:15:57,210 --> 00:16:01,250
but doing this practice out on the court
would be so much more effective...

280
00:16:03,290 --> 00:16:04,610
A training camp?

281
00:16:04,610 --> 00:16:05,750
Yes.

282
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:08,330
This weekend is the start 
of the Golden Week holiday,

283
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:10,920
so there's only one month left
until the inter-high prelims begin.

284
00:16:11,130 --> 00:16:13,460
We absolutely cannot afford
to let this opportunity pass us by.

285
00:16:14,170 --> 00:16:17,170
Are we seriously going to practice
through the entire holiday?

286
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:21,660
So like, is the inter-high just impossible for us
without doing all this work?

287
00:16:22,130 --> 00:16:24,790
In order for Kuzu High to 
actually reach the inter-high,

288
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:29,330
we must win the prelims and become
a representative team for the Kanagawa region.

289
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:34,380
Knockout League

290
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:34,380
Win

291
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:34,380
Lose

292
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:34,380
Score

293
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:34,380
Rank

294
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:32,250
The knockout league that decides
the representative teams

295
00:16:32,250 --> 00:16:34,630
consists of 4 schools that 
survive the prefectural prelims.

296
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:37,230
And to even enter the prefectural prelims,

297
00:16:37,230 --> 00:16:39,470
we first have claim victory in the district tournament.

298
00:16:40,130 --> 00:16:42,730
Out of hundreds of schools, there are only 2
who can become representatives

299
00:16:42,730 --> 00:16:43,940
for the inter-high.

300
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:49,580
The number of victories required to become
a representative team is 10, at the very least.

301
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:54,990
I believe that it would be difficult for our team
to even win a single game as we are now.

302
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:57,540
It just never ends...

303
00:16:57,750 --> 00:17:01,960
Now, now, now... There's always
a bright side to find, gentlemen.

304
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:04,040
It's Golden Week...

305
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:06,050
Places like the Nasu Highlands or Karuizawa are

306
00:17:06,050 --> 00:17:08,540
probably booked full with students from university clubs.

307
00:17:09,290 --> 00:17:11,960
And at this time, the beaches of Okinawa
should be open for swimming.

308
00:17:12,670 --> 00:17:15,710
Just imagine what it would be like
to have our training camp in a place like that.

309
00:17:16,380 --> 00:17:18,710
Oh... Okinawa...

310
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:36,080
YES! YES! YES!

311
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,670
A training camp, huh?

312
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:38,790
That's a solid idea for us to 
start refining our teamwork.

313
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:41,210
We swear to survive whatever harsh 
training they can throw at us!

314
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:42,040
Each of us will need to level 
up our individual skills, too.

315
00:17:42,210 --> 00:17:44,000
Awesome...

316
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,920
Being able to spend a whole day on basketball
is like a dream!

317
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:49,000
That sums it up, Mr. Satsuki.

318
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:54,380
Okinawa Okinawa! Okinawa!

319
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,200
Can you reserve a location for the camp and work the expenses into our budget?

320
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:54,380
Budget?

321
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,840
There's no budget for this team.

322
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:59,550
No... No way!

323
00:18:00,210 --> 00:18:03,330
The basketball team was nothing
but a hangout for hoodlums until recently.

324
00:18:03,330 --> 00:18:05,790
The school would never provide
any money considering that.

325
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:09,460
No budget... not even a single yen?

326
00:18:09,670 --> 00:18:12,170
If we file a formal application,
then there might be a chance.

327
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:14,250
But I expect it would just 
be a drop in the bucket.

328
00:18:14,250 --> 00:18:16,420
Okay then, boys...

329
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,960
...we have no choice but to 
fall back on our last resort!

330
00:18:21,790 --> 00:18:23,210
Work for the money!

331
00:18:21,790 --> 00:18:23,710
SAFETY
FIRST

332
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,330
These are way too heavy!

333
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,960
Kanagawa School of Medical Science
Secondary Hospital

334
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:04,620
I don't wanna drink it!

335
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:09,750
The reason you aren't getting any taller
is because you're always so picky like that, Sora.

336
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:14,090
But it's so white and yucky! 
And yucky and white!

337
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,710
Oh really?

338
00:19:15,710 --> 00:19:17,790
Well I happen to love it.

339
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:20,420
I've been drinking it ever 
since I was a little kid.

340
00:19:20,710 --> 00:19:23,580
That makes you living proof 
that this stuff doesn't work.

341
00:19:23,750 --> 00:19:26,250
I'll never get any taller by drinking it!

342
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,670
That's it, Sora. No dinner for you tonight!

343
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:32,290
What?! That's abuse! Tyranny!

344
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:35,080
I'm gonna call child protective services!

345
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:43,210
What's wrong? Did your bike get a flat tire?

346
00:19:43,830 --> 00:19:46,130
Oh crap! It's already past 6!

347
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:48,580
And I've still got half 
of them left to deliver!

348
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:53,830
Say, Miss, are you a nurse here?

349
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:55,540
Yes, I am.

350
00:19:55,790 --> 00:19:58,210
I-in the third ward...

351
00:19:58,210 --> 00:19:59,010
Huh?

352
00:19:59,010 --> 00:20:01,920
No, nevermind. Just forget it.

353
00:20:02,630 --> 00:20:04,300
Here. Please drink this!

354
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:04,300
Thunder Brand
Milk

355
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,460
Thanks for your hard work!

356
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:07,460
See ya!

357
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:09,040
Huh? Um, hey, wait kid!

358
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,080
Gotta hurry!

359
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:19,830
YUKA KURUMATANI

360
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,530
Hm? Is this milk?

361
00:20:22,530 --> 00:20:24,040
Oh, yeah.

362
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:28,490
I don't know why, but a small delivery boy
gave it to me. As a gift.

363
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:32,290
It seemed like maybe someone he knew
was hospitalized here.

364
00:20:35,250 --> 00:20:37,420
From: Sora
G'morning.

365
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,420
Excuse me, Ms. Yabuuchi?

366
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:40,080
Yes?

367
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,880
If it's all right with 
you, could I have this?

368
00:20:43,420 --> 00:20:46,080
I love a nice glass of milk!

369
00:20:51,210 --> 00:20:54,730
Forget about Okinawa,
this amount wouldn't even get us to Shonan.

370
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:58,940
Well, that's about the best we could hope for
from only a day's worth of work.

371
00:20:58,940 --> 00:20:59,920
Hold up.

372
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:02,490
Don't go forgetting about us now.

373
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:07,460
Just wait and see. We'll bring back over 10 times
your investment in an hour, tops!

374
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,290
Sorry!

375
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,410
You goddamn idiots!

376
00:21:14,870 --> 00:21:17,420
Did you guys forget that 
you're still in high school?!

377
00:21:17,420 --> 00:21:20,840
Just be patient and let Mr. Satsuki and I
handle our funding issues!

378
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:24,280
For the time being, Mr. Satsuki was kind enough

379
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:26,470
to provide us with some money from his own pocket!

380
00:21:28,170 --> 00:21:29,010
Okay, fam!

381
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:32,380
The beautiful shores of 
Okinawa are waiting for us!

382
00:21:32,630 --> 00:21:34,000
YES!

383
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,500
Yeah... about that.

384
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:40,420
Our training camp will be 
held entirely here at school.

385
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:44,630
By the way, in order to cut 
costs as much as possible,

386
00:21:43,290 --> 00:21:47,830
Training Camp Requirements
Cost - 3,000 yen per person
Rice - 3kg per person
Fresh veggies, fish, etc
(everyone brings what they can)
Futons - BYO
Fresh clothes - pair for every day
Snacks - up to 300-yen worth

387
00:21:44,630 --> 00:21:47,630
we will be responsible for preparing everything
that we feasibly can!

388
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:51,500
This is starting to sound more
like a survival camp than a training camp.

389
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:54,920
Excuse me... I'd like to 
withdraw from participating.

390
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:55,790
Request denied!

391
00:21:56,290 --> 00:21:59,460
We're all in this together, 
so let's do our best!

392
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:18,630
Doredake sora o miagetatte

393
00:22:18,630 --> 00:22:21,920
Boku wa tobenai to kimi wa itta

394
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:25,130
Ato nankai te o nobaseba

395
00:22:25,290 --> 00:22:28,500
Todoku no darou to naita yoru

396
00:22:28,630 --> 00:22:32,000
Nigedasu koto ni nareteitte

397
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:35,290
Sore ga yowasa dato shitta ano hi

398
00:22:35,290 --> 00:22:39,500
Hajimeyou mata, kyou kara

399
00:22:42,130 --> 00:22:48,130
Taisetsu na mono wa itsudemo soba ni atta

400
00:22:48,130 --> 00:22:54,460
Bokura wa itsumo hitori janai donna toki mo

401
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:57,790
Toberu sa doko made mo kimi wa

402
00:22:57,790 --> 00:23:01,540
Dare yori tataku tataku habataite

403
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:05,790
Nagashita namida no kazu dake

404
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,750
Tsuyoku narunda

405
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:11,070
Tsubasa hiroge sekai o megutte

406
00:23:11,070 --> 00:23:14,710
Dare mo shiranai mirai o sagasou

407
00:23:14,710 --> 00:23:19,290
Zutto, zutto, zutto

408
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:22,960
Aruite yukou saa, issho ni

409
00:23:30,970 --> 00:23:35,390
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Differing Enthusiasm

410
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:34,380
Next time: "Differing Enthusiasm."

